+
+## Usage reported to afterModelResponse
+
+- `afterModelResponse` receives usage covering every provider call in the turn, not the last one: a turn driven through two tool rounds reports each field summed across all three calls, so a deployer billing or auditing from this hook counts the round carrying the customer's question and the full tool results as well as the final leg ([validated by: reports usage covering every provider call in a turn driven through two tool rounds](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L67)).
+- A provider that reports no usage on some rounds does not turn what the hook receives into `undefined` or `NaN`: every round that did report is still counted, and a round that did not contributes nothing ([validated by: still counts the rounds that reported when a round reports no usage](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L79)).
+- A turn where no provider call reported usage still reports no usage: the hook receives `undefined`, not zeros ([validated by: reports no usage when no provider call in the turn reported one](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.usage.acceptance.test.ts#L91)).
